1
00:00:00,335 --> 00:00:03,575
Right now my leg is hanging through the ceiling over

2
00:00:03,575 --> 00:00:06,275
a hundred dead people, and my best friend is walking

3
00:00:06,275 --> 00:00:07,115
right under it.

4
00:00:07,317 --> 00:00:07,997
Stop moving.

5
00:00:08,552 --> 00:00:09,112
I stop.

6
00:00:09,912 --> 00:00:11,172
Another corner breaks off anyway.

7
00:00:14,330 --> 00:00:16,670
The woman on the radio asked who was in my

8
00:00:16,670 --> 00:00:19,690
daughter's window, and I gave her nothing. I took my

9
00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:20,590
thumb off the button.

10
00:00:21,390 --> 00:00:24,430
For six years, answering that radio had been my job.

11
00:00:24,890 --> 00:00:27,390
A call came in, I said my name, and whoever

12
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:29,250
was on the other end knew somebody was coming.

13
00:00:29,715 --> 00:00:31,775
Now I had to remind myself that I could leave

14
00:00:31,775 --> 00:00:34,475
it alone. My phone was in my other hand. No

15
00:00:34,475 --> 00:00:38,015
service. My mom's last message was still there, telling me

16
00:00:38,015 --> 00:00:40,235
the door was locked. I read it again while the

17
00:00:40,235 --> 00:00:43,435
woman waited. I wanted somebody to talk to badly enough

18
00:00:43,435 --> 00:00:45,175
that I was afraid of what I might say.

19
00:00:45,582 --> 00:00:48,922
Across the highway, the tenth-floor window stayed dark.

20
00:00:50,062 --> 00:00:51,862
Lily had already blinked three times.

21
00:00:52,642 --> 00:00:53,042
I'd answered.

22
00:00:54,082 --> 00:00:55,042
Our goodnight was over.

23
00:00:56,542 --> 00:00:58,722
The woman waited long enough that I could hear her

24
00:00:58,722 --> 00:01:00,282
breathing through the little speaker.

25
00:01:00,779 --> 00:01:01,039
Danny?

26
00:01:01,605 --> 00:01:05,065
I turned the volume down and held the radio against

27
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:05,605
my ear.

28
00:01:06,036 --> 00:01:06,716
You still there?

29
00:01:07,175 --> 00:01:10,415
I could see a faint light moving behind the department

30
00:01:10,415 --> 00:01:13,875
store's rooftop door. When I looked again, it was gone.

31
00:01:14,235 --> 00:01:16,935
I pressed the button. How did you get inside? A

32
00:01:16,935 --> 00:01:17,435
little laugh.

33
00:01:17,928 --> 00:01:20,008
That's a fairly rude first question.

34
00:01:20,643 --> 00:01:21,563
You asked me one.

35
00:01:22,098 --> 00:01:25,438
Fair enough. Vera. There. Now you have a name.

36
00:01:25,873 --> 00:01:26,393
I waited.

37
00:01:26,957 --> 00:01:30,497
I was trying on a coat. Department store. Second floor.

38
00:01:30,897 --> 00:01:33,597
Sat down in the fitting room and fell asleep. By

39
00:01:33,597 --> 00:01:35,877
the time I woke up, they'd locked the place.

40
00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:40,500
The store had closed at nine. At midnight,

41
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:43,780
I'd checked the staff corridor behind those fitting rooms. I'd

42
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:46,800
heard nothing. What coat? I asked.

43
00:01:47,201 --> 00:01:47,421
What?

44
00:01:47,946 --> 00:01:49,126
The one you were trying on.

45
00:01:49,594 --> 00:01:53,314
Danny, there are people eating people downstairs.

46
00:01:54,014 --> 00:01:56,554
I think we've moved beyond the returns policy.

47
00:01:57,214 --> 00:02:01,234
She sounded almost amused. Then her voice changed

48
00:02:01,234 --> 00:02:01,634
a little.

49
00:02:02,091 --> 00:02:05,451
There's a girl up here with me. She's hungry. Have

50
00:02:05,451 --> 00:02:06,631
you got anything we could eat?

51
00:02:07,147 --> 00:02:08,687
I looked at Lily's window again.

52
00:02:09,427 --> 00:02:11,227
Kept my thumb away from the button while I did

53
00:02:11,227 --> 00:02:12,127
it. How old?

54
00:02:12,486 --> 00:02:16,346
Little. Six, perhaps. Seven. It's hard to get much out

55
00:02:16,346 --> 00:02:16,586
of her.

56
00:02:16,928 --> 00:02:19,388
I stood on that roof until my hand went numb

57
00:02:19,388 --> 00:02:22,568
around the radio. Vera never asked about the window again

58
00:02:22,568 --> 00:02:25,508
that night. She'd found another question I couldn't walk away

59
00:02:25,508 --> 00:02:25,788
from.

60
00:02:27,139 --> 00:02:30,699
Somebody ate my breakfast while I slept inside a locked

61
00:02:30,699 --> 00:02:34,479
store. I'd put two protein bars beside the tent. One

62
00:02:34,479 --> 00:02:37,399
for when I woke up, one for later, because apparently

63
00:02:37,399 --> 00:02:40,279
I needed a system for deciding when to eat cardboard.

64
00:02:40,719 --> 00:02:43,799
There was one left. I checked the sleeping bag. Turned

65
00:02:43,799 --> 00:02:46,859
it inside out. Looked under the tent and inside both

66
00:02:46,859 --> 00:02:47,259
boots.

67
00:02:47,789 --> 00:02:51,309
At the gate, the padlock was closed. Key thirty-one was

68
00:02:51,309 --> 00:02:54,389
still on my belt. I counted the water twice. A

69
00:02:54,389 --> 00:02:57,429
bottle was missing too. I could explain losing a protein

70
00:02:57,429 --> 00:02:59,969
bar. I'd spent the night listening to my dead friend

71
00:02:59,969 --> 00:03:02,889
walk past, and my brain was doing its best to

72
00:03:02,889 --> 00:03:05,069
forget the whole thing. A bottle was harder.

73
00:03:05,583 --> 00:03:08,503
I lined everything up along the back wall. Bars in

74
00:03:08,503 --> 00:03:09,143
one row,

75
00:03:10,043 --> 00:03:13,383
cans in another, water underneath. Wrote the numbers on a

76
00:03:13,383 --> 00:03:15,623
receipt with the little pencil I used for my shift

77
00:03:15,623 --> 00:03:18,203
log. I hadn't written anything in that log since the

78
00:03:18,203 --> 00:03:18,703
first night.

79
00:03:19,068 --> 00:03:22,388
For a while I sat there trying to remember the

80
00:03:22,388 --> 00:03:26,368
last normal entry. A door propped open.

81
00:03:27,128 --> 00:03:29,588
A car parked across two spaces.

82
00:03:30,308 --> 00:03:33,178
Something I'd been annoyed about. Then I heard two pulls

83
00:03:33,348 --> 00:03:35,988
on a gate outside, and I remembered I was supposed

84
00:03:35,988 --> 00:03:36,988
to be counting water.

85
00:03:37,456 --> 00:03:41,396
I carried the remaining bars into the stockroom and put

86
00:03:41,396 --> 00:03:44,176
them in a plastic storage box. Then I sat beside

87
00:03:44,176 --> 00:03:47,176
it until my neck hurt. Nothing happened. At nine, I

88
00:03:47,176 --> 00:03:50,276
went to the roof. Three blinks from Lily. Three back

89
00:03:50,276 --> 00:03:53,116
from me. I kept my body between the flashlight and

90
00:03:53,116 --> 00:03:55,816
the department store. Vera called as soon as I came

91
00:03:55,816 --> 00:03:56,116
downstairs.

92
00:03:56,772 --> 00:03:57,912
Any luck with supper?

93
00:03:58,464 --> 00:03:59,804
I haven't agreed to anything.

94
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:01,645
You sound tired.

95
00:04:02,290 --> 00:04:03,770
I am tired.

96
00:04:04,546 --> 00:04:06,726
Get some rest. We can talk tomorrow.

97
00:04:07,231 --> 00:04:10,651
I stared at the storage box for another hour. When

98
00:04:10,651 --> 00:04:13,731
I finally slept, I put it beside my head. When

99
00:04:13,731 --> 00:04:16,411
I woke again, the lid was back on. One of

100
00:04:16,411 --> 00:04:18,391
the catches hadn't quite clicked shut.

101
00:04:19,431 --> 00:04:20,851
Two more bars were gone.

102
00:04:21,711 --> 00:04:24,171
Whoever was doing this had stood close enough to watch

103
00:04:24,171 --> 00:04:24,871
me sleep.

104
00:04:26,252 --> 00:04:28,412
The chalk came in a little white bag from the

105
00:04:28,412 --> 00:04:32,072
climbing display. I spread it around the food box, under

106
00:04:32,072 --> 00:04:35,492
the stockroom door, and across the narrow space between the

107
00:04:35,492 --> 00:04:37,652
tents. Then I went back to bed with my boots

108
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:37,932
on.

109
00:04:39,644 --> 00:04:41,704
That was my entire investigation.

110
00:04:42,424 --> 00:04:45,344
Six years in security, and I was waiting for somebody

111
00:04:45,344 --> 00:04:48,224
to step in powder. I left a fresh bar on

112
00:04:48,224 --> 00:04:50,384
top of the box. The rest went inside it.

113
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:53,800
I felt ridiculous setting bait with a breakfast I couldn't

114
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:56,420
afford to lose. But the gate was the only way

115
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:59,140
in that I understood. Whoever had found another way could

116
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:01,720
bring somebody else through it. I lay facing the gap

117
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:05,100
between the tents. If anybody came through there, this time

118
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:08,920
I'd see them. Sometime before morning, I heard plastic bend.

119
00:05:09,363 --> 00:05:11,663
By the time I'd got out of the sleeping bag,

120
00:05:12,063 --> 00:05:14,603
the store was still again. I left the overhead lights

121
00:05:14,603 --> 00:05:18,163
off and used my flashlight close to the floor. Small

122
00:05:18,163 --> 00:05:21,523
trainers. A worn patch under the right heel. The print

123
00:05:21,523 --> 00:05:24,043
had a little square of clear floor in the middle

124
00:05:24,043 --> 00:05:25,383
where the sole was split.

125
00:05:26,191 --> 00:05:29,951
The trail came from behind the climbing wall display. It

126
00:05:29,951 --> 00:05:33,151
went to the food box. Then it went back. I

127
00:05:33,151 --> 00:05:36,071
moved the display a few inches. Behind it was a

128
00:05:36,071 --> 00:05:39,511
tall storage rack bolted to the wall. A shoeprint showed

129
00:05:39,511 --> 00:05:42,571
on the bottom shelf. Another was pressed against the painted

130
00:05:42,571 --> 00:05:43,691
wall halfway up.

131
00:05:44,054 --> 00:05:48,034
Higher still, somebody had wiped a hand across a

132
00:05:48,034 --> 00:05:51,194
dusty pipe. I followed the pipe with the light. One

133
00:05:51,194 --> 00:05:54,734
ceiling tile was cleaner around the edges than all the

134
00:05:54,734 --> 00:05:57,894
others. I stood there with my mouth open. Every door

135
00:05:57,894 --> 00:06:01,544
was locked. Every window was intact. I'd checked the gates

136
00:06:01,634 --> 00:06:04,634
so often that morning my hand hurt. I hadn't looked

137
00:06:04,634 --> 00:06:05,514
up once.

138
00:06:06,091 --> 00:06:09,271
A little white flake dropped out of the seam above

139
00:06:09,271 --> 00:06:12,571
me. I switched the flashlight off. Whoever was up there

140
00:06:12,571 --> 00:06:14,891
had seen the light. And they were still there.

141
00:06:16,246 --> 00:06:18,966
I waited behind the display until my bad knee went

142
00:06:18,966 --> 00:06:22,546
stiff. It was barely six in the morning. Outside, Marcus

143
00:06:22,546 --> 00:06:25,966
rattled the gate and moved on. The tile lifted. Two

144
00:06:25,966 --> 00:06:29,806
fingers appeared, then a head, then a very skinny boy

145
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:31,906
lowering himself onto the top shelf.

146
00:06:32,372 --> 00:06:36,232
He moved carefully. He knew which bit of the rack

147
00:06:36,232 --> 00:06:39,132
squeaked. He stepped around it before his foot even touched

148
00:06:39,132 --> 00:06:41,892
down. When he reached the floor, he went straight to

149
00:06:41,892 --> 00:06:44,572
the box. I waited until he bent over it. Then

150
00:06:44,572 --> 00:06:46,772
I stood up. We looked at each other. He had

151
00:06:46,772 --> 00:06:48,792
a protein bar already in his hand.

152
00:06:49,198 --> 00:06:52,998
The sweatshirt hung past his fingers. There was a pale

153
00:06:52,998 --> 00:06:55,998
clean line around one wrist where he'd pushed a sleeve

154
00:06:55,998 --> 00:06:59,018
up. Everything else about him looked as dusty as the

155
00:06:59,018 --> 00:07:01,978
pipe. I'd practised this conversation in my head while I

156
00:07:01,978 --> 00:07:04,978
waited. It had involved a grown man explaining himself.

157
00:07:05,501 --> 00:07:08,081
I hadn't practised what to do if the thief looked

158
00:07:08,081 --> 00:07:11,121
hungry enough to eat the wrapper. Put it down, I

159
00:07:11,121 --> 00:07:13,761
said. He put it down. Then he ran straight at

160
00:07:13,761 --> 00:07:13,961
me.

161
00:07:14,306 --> 00:07:18,026
I moved aside because, for a second, that's what my

162
00:07:18,026 --> 00:07:20,306
body thought you did when a kid ran at you.

163
00:07:20,586 --> 00:07:23,486
He got past, took two steps up the rack, and

164
00:07:23,486 --> 00:07:25,926
nearly reached the pipe. I caught the back of his

165
00:07:25,926 --> 00:07:29,166
sweatshirt. He twisted so hard the stitching tore.

166
00:07:29,685 --> 00:07:30,105
Let go.

167
00:07:31,263 --> 00:07:32,163
Stop kicking.

168
00:07:32,670 --> 00:07:33,210
Let go.

169
00:07:33,637 --> 00:07:36,757
I did. He stayed on the second shelf, one hand

170
00:07:36,757 --> 00:07:38,577
on the pipe, watching my hands.

171
00:07:39,457 --> 00:07:43,077
The loose shelf knocked against the wall. Somewhere outside, a

172
00:07:43,077 --> 00:07:46,937
shoe dragged across the floor. We both stopped breathing. A

173
00:07:46,937 --> 00:07:49,797
shadow passed the gate. Paused. Moved on.

174
00:07:50,577 --> 00:07:52,837
The boy looked toward the hallway, then back at me.

175
00:07:53,191 --> 00:07:54,491
Don't do that again,

176
00:07:55,027 --> 00:07:55,607
he whispered.

177
00:07:56,327 --> 00:07:58,627
I wanted to tell him I was the adult and

178
00:07:58,627 --> 00:08:01,667
this was my store and he was stealing my food.

179
00:08:02,287 --> 00:08:03,487
Instead I asked how old he was.

180
00:08:03,922 --> 00:08:04,383
Fifteen.

181
00:08:05,067 --> 00:08:05,607
Your name?

182
00:08:06,054 --> 00:08:06,254
Theo.

183
00:08:06,872 --> 00:08:09,452
Who else is up there? He tightened his grip on

184
00:08:09,452 --> 00:08:09,812
the pipe.

185
00:08:10,276 --> 00:08:12,236
Nobody. That's why I stay up there.

186
00:08:13,631 --> 00:08:16,531
I let him sit on an overturned camping bucket. He

187
00:08:16,531 --> 00:08:18,971
kept the rack within reach. Where do you sleep?

188
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:20,300
Above the cinema.

189
00:08:21,556 --> 00:08:22,676
In the ceiling?

190
00:08:23,263 --> 00:08:25,463
There's a space beside the projection room.

191
00:08:25,849 --> 00:08:29,269
For four months? He shrugged. A tiny movement.

192
00:08:29,649 --> 00:08:32,509
Like he was trying to make four months smaller. How

193
00:08:32,509 --> 00:08:32,989
did you eat?

194
00:08:33,458 --> 00:08:34,938
People throw stuff out.

195
00:08:35,301 --> 00:08:35,801
And the doors?

196
00:08:36,386 --> 00:08:37,286
I go round them.

197
00:08:37,711 --> 00:08:40,691
I looked up at the tile again. He pointed toward

198
00:08:40,691 --> 00:08:41,171
my belt.

199
00:08:41,649 --> 00:08:42,629
You like checking those.

200
00:08:43,134 --> 00:08:44,174
The keys?

201
00:08:45,218 --> 00:08:48,318
The doors. You do the same ones twice when you're

202
00:08:48,318 --> 00:08:48,858
on the phone.

203
00:08:49,326 --> 00:08:51,926
I thought about all the nights I'd walked this building,

204
00:08:52,526 --> 00:08:56,566
tugged handles, signed the log, and told myself everybody was

205
00:08:56,566 --> 00:08:59,646
safe. Theo peeled a strip of tape away from his

206
00:08:59,646 --> 00:09:01,346
trainer. Pressed it back down.

207
00:09:01,746 --> 00:09:03,266
You sing in the freight elevator,

208
00:09:03,887 --> 00:09:05,467
he said. I looked at him.

209
00:09:05,806 --> 00:09:09,226
Usually the same song. You only know some of it.

210
00:09:09,529 --> 00:09:13,449
My face got hot. Even then. Even with everything outside,

211
00:09:13,929 --> 00:09:16,689
that still worked. You can't stay here, I said.

212
00:09:17,749 --> 00:09:21,509
The words came out before I'd decided what I meant

213
00:09:21,509 --> 00:09:24,349
by them. There were two sentences in my head. One

214
00:09:24,349 --> 00:09:26,659
was about food. The other was about the man who'd

215
00:09:26,769 --> 00:09:29,129
sat outside my gate and trusted me to know what

216
00:09:29,129 --> 00:09:29,409
to do.

217
00:09:29,660 --> 00:09:32,540
I could hardly look at that gate in daylight. Now

218
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:35,260
this kid was sitting six feet from it, waiting for

219
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:39,140
me to be in charge. I wanted somebody qualified. A

220
00:09:39,140 --> 00:09:42,860
firefighter. His dad. Any adult who'd know how to keep

221
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:45,680
him alive. He was looking at the only one available.

222
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:47,220
Theo stood immediately.

223
00:09:47,776 --> 00:09:51,336
He didn't argue. Picked up nothing, because he'd brought nothing.

224
00:09:51,696 --> 00:09:54,516
I heard Marcus at another gate down the hall. Theo

225
00:09:54,516 --> 00:09:57,616
heard him too. Wait, I said. He waited beside the

226
00:09:57,616 --> 00:10:00,676
rack. I reached for a bottle, then stopped with my

227
00:10:00,676 --> 00:10:03,196
hand on it. Theo watched me count the ones left.

228
00:10:03,656 --> 00:10:04,536
How long have you got?

229
00:10:04,891 --> 00:10:08,231
he asked. About ten days. Maybe. I was working it

230
00:10:08,231 --> 00:10:10,351
out for one person. He looked toward the front of

231
00:10:10,351 --> 00:10:10,611
the mall.

232
00:10:11,009 --> 00:10:13,069
I know where there's eight thousand gallons.

233
00:10:14,674 --> 00:10:15,134
The fountain,

234
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:17,678
Theo said. I stared at him.

235
00:10:18,002 --> 00:10:19,042
Big tank underneath,

236
00:10:19,634 --> 00:10:20,414
Theo said.

237
00:10:20,864 --> 00:10:24,584
There's a room with all the pumps. Number's written on

238
00:10:24,584 --> 00:10:25,044
the side.

239
00:10:25,485 --> 00:10:29,085
Eight thousand? He nodded. I knew the pump-room door.

240
00:10:29,485 --> 00:10:32,345
It opened into the center court, beside the pretzel place.

241
00:10:32,745 --> 00:10:36,225
On the cameras, that doorway was buried behind bodies.

242
00:10:36,625 --> 00:10:38,025
The way downstairs is full.

243
00:10:38,465 --> 00:10:39,445
I come from above.

244
00:10:39,988 --> 00:10:42,388
He drew a route in the chalk with one finger.

245
00:10:43,608 --> 00:10:47,208
Above the cinema. Across a service walkway. Down inside the

246
00:10:47,208 --> 00:10:50,428
big column beside the fountain, on a maintenance ladder. The

247
00:10:50,428 --> 00:10:53,348
route ended behind the locked pump-room door. I could feel

248
00:10:53,348 --> 00:10:55,428
the weight of the keys on my hip. Why haven't

249
00:10:55,428 --> 00:10:56,108
you gone already?

250
00:10:56,567 --> 00:10:57,907
Nothing to carry it in.

251
00:10:58,289 --> 00:11:02,169
The store around us was full of camping water

252
00:11:02,169 --> 00:11:02,669
containers.

253
00:11:03,469 --> 00:11:06,629
How much can you carry back? I asked. He held

254
00:11:06,629 --> 00:11:08,249
his hands a little apart.

255
00:11:08,723 --> 00:11:09,503
Small ones.

256
00:11:10,263 --> 00:11:11,323
You have to get them through.

257
00:11:11,895 --> 00:11:13,515
We settled on two smaller ones.

258
00:11:13,953 --> 00:11:17,693
Theo watched without saying anything. I wished he'd made a

259
00:11:17,693 --> 00:11:20,713
joke. It would've been easier than watching him decide whether

260
00:11:20,713 --> 00:11:23,153
I could do it. He looked at them. Looked at

261
00:11:23,153 --> 00:11:26,573
me. We understood each other then. I'd been counting bottles

262
00:11:26,573 --> 00:11:29,753
and locking gates. He'd been counting routes through walls.

263
00:11:30,299 --> 00:11:33,479
That night Vera called again. She said the little girl

264
00:11:33,479 --> 00:11:36,859
had stopped asking for food. I held the radio so

265
00:11:36,859 --> 00:11:38,839
tightly the plastic creaked.

266
00:11:39,239 --> 00:11:40,539
Get some sleep, Danny,

267
00:11:41,152 --> 00:11:41,612
she said.

268
00:11:42,006 --> 00:11:43,286
You'll think better tomorrow.

269
00:11:43,927 --> 00:11:47,587
I sat beside Theo's bucket after the light went out.

270
00:11:47,907 --> 00:11:50,887
Show me the way, I said. We bring water back.

271
00:11:51,327 --> 00:11:54,007
You get food. We work the rest out after. He

272
00:11:54,007 --> 00:11:55,727
looked at the tent, then at the rack.

273
00:11:56,205 --> 00:11:58,455
My mom had gone into the apartment with about ten

274
00:11:58,665 --> 00:12:01,645
days of insulin. Every time I counted my water, I

275
00:12:01,645 --> 00:12:03,705
found myself counting her days too.

276
00:12:04,114 --> 00:12:07,474
Getting more water wouldn't get me across the highway. But

277
00:12:07,474 --> 00:12:10,354
I couldn't do anything for either of them if I

278
00:12:10,354 --> 00:12:12,494
spent the next week getting too weak to climb the

279
00:12:12,494 --> 00:12:12,974
roof ladder.

280
00:12:13,443 --> 00:12:14,083
You coming too?

281
00:12:14,490 --> 00:12:17,170
Yes. He glanced at my boots. That was when I

282
00:12:17,170 --> 00:12:19,230
started worrying about what his route could hold.

283
00:12:20,607 --> 00:12:23,247
We left before the mall got bright. I took empty

284
00:12:23,247 --> 00:12:26,947
camping containers, a flashlight, and a strap from the climbing

285
00:12:26,947 --> 00:12:30,187
display. I took the battery out of Marcus's radio. Wrapped

286
00:12:30,187 --> 00:12:32,367
the keyring in a sock so the metal would stay

287
00:12:32,367 --> 00:12:32,707
quiet.

288
00:12:33,229 --> 00:12:36,509
Theo made me try the rack without the containers first.

289
00:12:36,929 --> 00:12:39,209
On the second shelf I reached for something that looked

290
00:12:39,209 --> 00:12:41,849
solid. He caught my hand before I put any weight

291
00:12:41,849 --> 00:12:42,209
on it.

292
00:12:42,534 --> 00:12:44,234
That's for holding the ceiling up,

293
00:12:44,668 --> 00:12:45,208
he said.

294
00:12:45,704 --> 00:12:46,684
It won't hold you.

295
00:12:47,082 --> 00:12:50,762
He moved my hand to a thick support above it.

296
00:12:51,202 --> 00:12:53,800
I nodded as if I'd understood that all along.

297
00:12:54,003 --> 00:12:55,173
You always carry that many?

298
00:12:55,625 --> 00:12:56,645
Every night.

299
00:12:56,974 --> 00:12:57,854
Must've been annoying.

300
00:12:58,410 --> 00:13:01,770
It had been. I would've given almost anything to be

301
00:13:01,770 --> 00:13:04,770
annoyed by that sound again on an ordinary Tuesday.

302
00:13:05,830 --> 00:13:09,010
Above the store, the air was warm and smelled like

303
00:13:09,010 --> 00:13:12,030
dust from a heater somebody had just switched on. Theo

304
00:13:12,030 --> 00:13:13,870
showed me where the metal supports ran.

305
00:13:14,284 --> 00:13:17,964
I followed them on my hands and knees. Kept my

306
00:13:17,964 --> 00:13:21,344
weight on the heavy steel. The ceiling tiles shifted below

307
00:13:21,344 --> 00:13:24,704
us when I breathed too hard. Over the cinema, he

308
00:13:24,704 --> 00:13:28,104
stopped beside a stained blanket. There were three empty water

309
00:13:28,104 --> 00:13:32,224
bottles, a folded hoodie, and a photograph turned

310
00:13:32,224 --> 00:13:35,264
face down. He slid that underneath the blanket before I

311
00:13:35,264 --> 00:13:35,784
could see it.

312
00:13:36,152 --> 00:13:40,432
A door beside the little platform had CINEMA SERVICE stencilled

313
00:13:40,952 --> 00:13:44,372
across it. Key seventeen fit. Theo watched the lock turn

314
00:13:44,372 --> 00:13:46,832
as though I'd done a trick. You've been climbing around

315
00:13:46,832 --> 00:13:47,112
this?

316
00:13:47,544 --> 00:13:48,184
For a while.

317
00:13:48,719 --> 00:13:51,159
I opened it just wide enough for us to get

318
00:13:51,159 --> 00:13:54,419
through. On the other side was the service walkway over

319
00:13:54,419 --> 00:13:57,359
the center court. Through gaps beneath the rail, I could

320
00:13:57,359 --> 00:13:58,539
see the tops of heads.

321
00:13:59,239 --> 00:14:02,859
Theo stepped out first. Halfway across, the proper walkway ended.

322
00:14:03,219 --> 00:14:05,799
Beyond it, the route followed a pair of supports above

323
00:14:05,799 --> 00:14:07,819
the suspended ceiling. I stopped.

324
00:14:08,293 --> 00:14:09,253
Theo looked back.

325
00:14:09,740 --> 00:14:12,560
Don't put your foot where you think the floor is.

326
00:14:13,984 --> 00:14:17,684
My best friend walked his rounds while I crawled over

327
00:14:17,684 --> 00:14:18,144
his head.

328
00:14:19,084 --> 00:14:21,664
Theo crossed the first gap easily. I watched where his

329
00:14:21,664 --> 00:14:23,964
hands went, then tried to put mine in the same

330
00:14:23,964 --> 00:14:24,404
places.

331
00:14:25,244 --> 00:14:28,564
There was a difference between watching a skinny fifteen-year-old do

332
00:14:28,564 --> 00:14:31,264
something and asking my knees to do it afterward.

333
00:14:31,827 --> 00:14:34,687
Sweat ran down my nose. I caught it on my

334
00:14:34,687 --> 00:14:37,727
sleeve before it could fall. One of the emergency lights

335
00:14:37,727 --> 00:14:41,107
flickered underneath us. For a second the shadows moved and

336
00:14:41,107 --> 00:14:44,027
I tightened both hands on the steel. Theo stopped with

337
00:14:44,027 --> 00:14:45,467
me. He didn't tell me to hurry.

338
00:14:45,851 --> 00:14:46,511
Next hand,

339
00:14:46,968 --> 00:14:48,628
he whispered. I moved it.

340
00:14:48,881 --> 00:14:49,761
Now your knee.

341
00:14:50,209 --> 00:14:52,929
I moved that too. After a while I could do

342
00:14:52,929 --> 00:14:56,089
two movements without being told. I was grateful he didn't

343
00:14:56,089 --> 00:14:59,389
mention it. Below us, the fountain was dark. Coins lay

344
00:14:59,389 --> 00:15:02,049
on the bottom. The people around it were standing shoulder

345
00:15:02,049 --> 00:15:05,179
to shoulder in places, their faces turned toward the food-court

346
00:15:05,409 --> 00:15:07,429
doors. I stopped counting at a hundred.

347
00:15:07,823 --> 00:15:11,123
Theo reached back for a container. I passed it forward.

348
00:15:11,483 --> 00:15:13,863
He put it on a solid section, then came back

349
00:15:13,863 --> 00:15:17,103
for the other one. Slow. Everything had to be slow.

350
00:15:17,443 --> 00:15:19,283
A gate rattled at the far end of the hall.

351
00:15:19,623 --> 00:15:21,403
I knew who it was before I saw him.

352
00:15:21,712 --> 00:15:24,392
Marcus came around the corner and stopped at the first

353
00:15:24,392 --> 00:15:27,572
store. Two pulls on the gate. A pause. Then the

354
00:15:27,572 --> 00:15:29,872
next one. I found myself waiting for him to look

355
00:15:29,872 --> 00:15:32,852
up. Theo touched my shoulder. I moved my knee to

356
00:15:32,852 --> 00:15:35,212
give him room. The bit of metal under it folded.

357
00:15:35,702 --> 00:15:38,782
I dropped far enough that my stomach hit the edge

358
00:15:38,782 --> 00:15:41,562
of the support. My right leg punched through a tile.

359
00:15:42,042 --> 00:15:44,282
Something caught the leather of my boot and held it

360
00:15:44,282 --> 00:15:47,282
there. Pieces fell into the court. The first one struck

361
00:15:47,282 --> 00:15:49,842
the fountain's rim. A head turned. Then another.

362
00:15:50,328 --> 00:15:53,048
Theo caught my wrist. I tried to pull my knee

363
00:15:53,048 --> 00:15:56,528
back, and a sharp edge dug into my thigh. Below,

364
00:15:56,748 --> 00:16:00,028
Marcus stopped walking. He lifted his face toward my foot.

365
00:16:00,408 --> 00:16:02,268
My boot began to slide off.

366
00:16:03,731 --> 00:16:06,271
The kid I'd told to leave was the only thing

367
00:16:06,271 --> 00:16:09,591
keeping me out of that crowd. Theo lay flat and

368
00:16:09,591 --> 00:16:12,511
reached for my other wrist. His fingers slipped on my

369
00:16:12,511 --> 00:16:12,891
sleeve.

370
00:16:13,381 --> 00:16:14,141
Give me your hand.

371
00:16:14,610 --> 00:16:15,810
I tried.

372
00:16:16,650 --> 00:16:19,610
A long piece of the tile broke away and hit

373
00:16:19,610 --> 00:16:20,490
someone's shoulder.

374
00:16:21,530 --> 00:16:23,330
People began pushing under the hole.

375
00:16:24,670 --> 00:16:28,390
Slowly, one body leaning into the next. Marcus stood among

376
00:16:28,390 --> 00:16:29,590
them, looking up.

377
00:16:29,981 --> 00:16:32,581
I could see the worn patch on his cap. I'd

378
00:16:32,581 --> 00:16:35,161
stood beside him in the office while he picked at

379
00:16:35,161 --> 00:16:37,721
it with his thumbnail and told me a joke I'd

380
00:16:37,721 --> 00:16:40,901
already heard. I nearly said his name. Theo hit my

381
00:16:40,901 --> 00:16:41,201
arm.

382
00:16:41,601 --> 00:16:42,061
Look at me.

383
00:16:42,429 --> 00:16:44,969
I looked up. He was reaching for the strap I'd

384
00:16:44,969 --> 00:16:48,449
brought. Getting it around the heavy support with one hand

385
00:16:48,449 --> 00:16:49,989
while the other held my sleeve.

386
00:16:50,561 --> 00:16:51,801
You have to let go,

387
00:16:52,352 --> 00:16:52,952
he whispered.

388
00:16:53,712 --> 00:16:54,712
I shook my head.

389
00:16:55,166 --> 00:16:56,966
One hand. I need the strap.

390
00:16:57,378 --> 00:16:58,098
His

391
00:16:58,818 --> 00:17:00,698
sleeve was bunched in my fist.

392
00:17:01,778 --> 00:17:03,978
I'd been holding him so hard the cloth had twisted

393
00:17:03,978 --> 00:17:04,798
around his arm.

394
00:17:05,618 --> 00:17:08,078
I made myself open my fingers. He fed the strap

395
00:17:08,078 --> 00:17:10,518
around the support and leaned his weight into it. I

396
00:17:10,518 --> 00:17:13,758
heard fabric pull tight. His shoe slipped against the brace,

397
00:17:13,758 --> 00:17:15,878
and he caught himself with a sharp little breath.

398
00:17:16,340 --> 00:17:19,120
Then his hand was back in front of my face.

399
00:17:19,600 --> 00:17:20,340
Elbow up,

400
00:17:20,895 --> 00:17:21,295
he said.

401
00:17:21,910 --> 00:17:22,670
You have to help.

402
00:17:23,145 --> 00:17:26,845
I got an elbow onto the steel. Pushed until my

403
00:17:26,845 --> 00:17:30,245
shoulder felt as though it was coming apart. Theo leaned

404
00:17:30,245 --> 00:17:33,545
back against the strap and pulled. My boot stayed where

405
00:17:33,545 --> 00:17:36,265
it was. My foot came out of it. For a

406
00:17:36,265 --> 00:17:37,885
second I thought that meant I was falling.

407
00:17:38,423 --> 00:17:42,143
Then my knee slid over the edge, and Theo dragged

408
00:17:42,143 --> 00:17:45,003
me onto the solid platform with him. We lay there

409
00:17:45,003 --> 00:17:49,323
together, breathing into our sleeves. Below us, the boot finally

410
00:17:49,323 --> 00:17:52,483
came loose. It landed inside the empty fountain with a

411
00:17:52,483 --> 00:17:55,603
noise that seemed to go on forever. Theo pressed both

412
00:17:55,603 --> 00:17:57,243
palms against the metal and waited.

413
00:17:57,719 --> 00:18:01,559
Eventually the pushing slowed. A few faces

414
00:18:01,559 --> 00:18:04,959
turned away. I looked at him. His trouser leg was

415
00:18:04,959 --> 00:18:08,599
torn at the calf. There was blood on the sharp

416
00:18:08,599 --> 00:18:11,299
brace he'd crawled across to reach me. He pulled the

417
00:18:11,299 --> 00:18:12,339
fabric down over it.

418
00:18:12,718 --> 00:18:14,638
You can walk without that shoe,

419
00:18:15,098 --> 00:18:19,738
he whispered. Somewhere ahead and below us, water dripped.

420
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:24,280
The maintenance ladder ran down inside the service column. At

421
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:27,180
the bottom, a narrow hatch opened into the pump room

422
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:27,840
beneath the fountain.

423
00:18:28,321 --> 00:18:31,701
I put my good foot on each rung first. Theo

424
00:18:31,701 --> 00:18:34,381
stayed close enough to hear every breath I was trying

425
00:18:34,381 --> 00:18:36,821
to keep quiet. The tank took up most of the

426
00:18:36,821 --> 00:18:40,581
room. EIGHT THOUSAND GALLONS was printed on a plate beside

427
00:18:40,581 --> 00:18:43,481
its inspection window. There was water behind the glass.

428
00:18:43,951 --> 00:18:47,091
I put my hand against the tank and left it

429
00:18:47,091 --> 00:18:49,051
there for a while. We still had to get it

430
00:18:49,051 --> 00:18:51,471
back and treat it with the gear in the store.

431
00:18:52,271 --> 00:18:54,591
But I could stop staring at the last few bottles

432
00:18:54,591 --> 00:18:55,671
every time I swallowed.

433
00:18:56,571 --> 00:18:59,661
Theo eased himself onto the bottom rung. He was favouring

434
00:18:59,831 --> 00:19:01,451
his leg. You hurt?

435
00:19:01,898 --> 00:19:02,378
Caught it.

436
00:19:02,692 --> 00:19:03,232
I saw.

437
00:19:03,768 --> 00:19:04,668
Then why'd you ask?

438
00:19:05,117 --> 00:19:08,197
I nearly smiled. We filled what we could carry.

439
00:19:08,957 --> 00:19:12,017
The handles pulled at my fingers when I lifted the

440
00:19:12,017 --> 00:19:12,437
containers.

441
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:16,717
We'd be drinking what we carried back for days. After

442
00:19:16,717 --> 00:19:19,737
that, we'd have to come again. The thought of that

443
00:19:19,737 --> 00:19:21,837
crossing again made me put one down.

444
00:19:22,617 --> 00:19:23,117
Theo noticed.

445
00:19:23,613 --> 00:19:25,613
We can find a better bit to cross,

446
00:19:26,225 --> 00:19:26,725
he said.

447
00:19:27,605 --> 00:19:28,385
You know one?

448
00:19:28,828 --> 00:19:29,428
I can look.

449
00:19:30,045 --> 00:19:33,485
I held the handle again. He'd spent four months figuring

450
00:19:33,485 --> 00:19:35,485
this place out because he had to.

451
00:19:36,205 --> 00:19:37,905
I was going to have to start doing the same.

452
00:19:38,665 --> 00:19:42,285
Outside the pump-room door, a shoe scraped along the floor.

453
00:19:42,685 --> 00:19:45,785
Dust shook out of the frame. Theo stared at that

454
00:19:45,785 --> 00:19:46,045
door.

455
00:19:46,462 --> 00:19:47,502
This is where they were,

456
00:19:47,990 --> 00:19:49,290
he said. Who?

457
00:19:49,775 --> 00:19:50,555
The drill people.

458
00:19:51,136 --> 00:19:52,816
I set the container down.

459
00:19:53,203 --> 00:19:56,463
Three of them. A woman and two men. Behind the

460
00:19:56,463 --> 00:19:58,203
pretzel place. First night.

461
00:19:58,563 --> 00:19:59,543
What time?

462
00:20:00,084 --> 00:20:02,964
One-thirty. I could see the clock through the opening.

463
00:20:03,388 --> 00:20:07,068
One-thirty. Ten minutes before Marcus called about the man on

464
00:20:07,068 --> 00:20:07,428
the ramp.

465
00:20:07,837 --> 00:20:09,137
They were cutting through the wall,

466
00:20:09,547 --> 00:20:10,187
Theo said.

467
00:20:10,650 --> 00:20:13,510
Loud as a chainsaw. I could hear it all the

468
00:20:13,510 --> 00:20:14,230
way at the cinema.

469
00:20:14,733 --> 00:20:16,513
He rubbed his sleeve over his nose.

470
00:20:17,069 --> 00:20:20,489
People started coming in. Through the service hall. They just

471
00:20:20,489 --> 00:20:21,089
kept coming.

472
00:20:21,583 --> 00:20:23,163
What did the woman do?

473
00:20:23,647 --> 00:20:24,767
Told them to keep drilling.

474
00:20:26,181 --> 00:20:29,181
I sat on the bottom rung beside Theo. Through the

475
00:20:29,181 --> 00:20:32,461
door, I could hear somebody's hand dragging over the wall.

476
00:20:32,681 --> 00:20:34,481
The woman on my radio? I asked.

477
00:20:34,906 --> 00:20:38,066
Same voice. I heard her in your store last night.

478
00:20:39,086 --> 00:20:39,746
You're sure?

479
00:20:40,238 --> 00:20:42,578
She was right below me when they were drilling, Danny.

480
00:20:43,323 --> 00:20:46,183
I looked at the door. They saw them? Theo nodded.

481
00:20:46,692 --> 00:20:49,032
One of the men went to look. Came back running.

482
00:20:49,452 --> 00:20:50,932
The woman kept saying another minute.

483
00:20:51,312 --> 00:20:52,512
And then?

484
00:20:52,815 --> 00:20:55,515
They took the machine and went through the staff door.

485
00:20:55,975 --> 00:20:57,895
I stayed where I was until it got quiet.

486
00:20:58,325 --> 00:21:00,845
The food court. The broken glass.

487
00:21:01,565 --> 00:21:04,765
The service halls filling up. I'd watched all those cameras

488
00:21:04,765 --> 00:21:07,445
and thought the crowd was wandering through any door it

489
00:21:07,445 --> 00:21:07,805
found.

490
00:21:08,645 --> 00:21:11,205
I'd been watching where they went. Theo had heard what

491
00:21:11,205 --> 00:21:13,905
they were following. Was there a kid with them? Theo

492
00:21:13,905 --> 00:21:15,545
shook his head. A little girl?

493
00:21:15,959 --> 00:21:16,199
No.

494
00:21:16,638 --> 00:21:20,218
I heard Vera's voice again. Soft through the speaker. The

495
00:21:20,218 --> 00:21:22,998
little girl had stopped asking for food. I stood up

496
00:21:22,998 --> 00:21:25,838
too fast and hit my shoulder on the ladder. Theo

497
00:21:25,838 --> 00:21:27,918
caught the container before it struck the floor.

498
00:21:28,333 --> 00:21:30,873
For a moment I wanted to go straight to the

499
00:21:30,873 --> 00:21:34,313
department store. Stand outside her gate and make her tell

500
00:21:34,313 --> 00:21:36,333
me why she'd kept that drill going.

501
00:21:37,113 --> 00:21:39,653
My keys were still wrapped in the sock. I closed

502
00:21:39,653 --> 00:21:42,253
my hand around them until the teeth pressed through the

503
00:21:42,253 --> 00:21:42,673
fabric.

504
00:21:43,101 --> 00:21:43,381
Danny,

505
00:21:43,947 --> 00:21:46,627
Theo said. I looked at his leg. At the blood

506
00:21:46,627 --> 00:21:49,067
drying on the edge of his trainer. He had followed

507
00:21:49,067 --> 00:21:51,107
me down here. Now he was waiting for me to

508
00:21:51,107 --> 00:21:53,207
get him back. I picked up the water. On the

509
00:21:53,207 --> 00:21:56,007
return trip, we moved around the broken section. It took

510
00:21:56,007 --> 00:21:58,287
nearly an hour. I could see my boot in the

511
00:21:58,287 --> 00:21:58,947
fountain below.

512
00:21:59,296 --> 00:22:00,676
I could see Marcus too.

513
00:22:02,967 --> 00:22:04,967
[metal strains]

514
00:22:09,367 --> 00:22:11,367
[water spills]

515
00:22:12,967 --> 00:22:14,967
[breathing, distant groans]

516
00:22:25,276 --> 00:22:27,696
At the cinema, Theo stopped to pick up his blanket.

517
00:22:28,016 --> 00:22:31,276
He tucked the photograph inside it. I pretended to be

518
00:22:31,276 --> 00:22:34,196
busy with the containers. I got back to Summit Outdoors

519
00:22:34,196 --> 00:22:37,496
in one boot and a filthy sock. Theo went down

520
00:22:37,496 --> 00:22:40,356
first and cleared a place for the containers. Then he

521
00:22:40,356 --> 00:22:41,816
steadied the rack while I climbed.

522
00:22:42,240 --> 00:22:44,620
I reached the floor and put my hand on the

523
00:22:44,620 --> 00:22:46,000
padlock. Closed.

524
00:22:46,760 --> 00:22:49,380
Exactly where I'd left it. I let go and turned

525
00:22:49,380 --> 00:22:52,200
toward Theo. He was sitting on the bucket, trying to

526
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:54,540
bend his trouser leg far enough to see the cut.

527
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:57,180
I'd checked that lock so many times.

528
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,780
Theo had just brought me home without going anywhere near

529
00:23:00,780 --> 00:23:01,040
it.

530
00:23:01,398 --> 00:23:04,898
I got the first-aid box. At nine, I climbed to

531
00:23:04,898 --> 00:23:05,598
the roof alone.

532
00:23:06,298 --> 00:23:08,238
Three lights from Lily. Three back.

533
00:23:09,038 --> 00:23:10,918
I held the roof hatch open a little on the

534
00:23:10,918 --> 00:23:13,258
way down, so I could see whether Theo was still

535
00:23:13,258 --> 00:23:15,438
there. He was asleep beside the water.

536
00:23:16,878 --> 00:23:20,018
We'd got back the afternoon before. I'd used bottled water

537
00:23:20,018 --> 00:23:22,278
to clean the scrape on his leg and found a

538
00:23:22,278 --> 00:23:24,758
bandage in the first-aid display. He'd let me do it

539
00:23:24,758 --> 00:23:26,098
without looking at me once.

540
00:23:26,629 --> 00:23:28,529
I'd asked him to tell me if it got worse.

541
00:23:29,409 --> 00:23:30,169
He'd said he would,

542
00:23:31,029 --> 00:23:34,949
much too quickly. Later, I'd found him putting the empty

543
00:23:34,949 --> 00:23:37,769
wrapper from his bandage inside another wrapper,

544
00:23:38,469 --> 00:23:41,789
folding both down until they took up almost no room.

545
00:23:42,249 --> 00:23:43,469
He'd done the same with his food.

546
00:23:44,002 --> 00:23:46,522
I knew that habit. I'd seen it in the places

547
00:23:46,522 --> 00:23:49,822
above the cinema. A whole life packed small enough that

548
00:23:49,822 --> 00:23:52,482
you could move it before somebody told you to. That

549
00:23:52,482 --> 00:23:55,042
morning he was beside the rack with his blanket rolled

550
00:23:55,042 --> 00:23:56,582
under one arm. Where are you going?

551
00:23:56,936 --> 00:23:57,416
Back.

552
00:23:57,916 --> 00:23:59,596
Your leg's hurting.

553
00:24:00,090 --> 00:24:00,830
It's fine.

554
00:24:01,311 --> 00:24:04,031
He shifted his weight onto the other foot. I looked

555
00:24:04,031 --> 00:24:07,091
at the ceiling tile. His way out was three shelves

556
00:24:07,091 --> 00:24:09,551
up, above the pipe he'd used while I slept.

557
00:24:10,311 --> 00:24:13,551
Pick a tent, I said. He watched me. Any of

558
00:24:13,551 --> 00:24:16,211
them. Except that one. I'm in that one.

559
00:24:16,514 --> 00:24:17,254
For how long?

560
00:24:17,687 --> 00:24:18,707
We'll work it out.

561
00:24:19,146 --> 00:24:19,846
What do you want?

562
00:24:20,318 --> 00:24:23,258
That question made me put down the box I was

563
00:24:23,258 --> 00:24:26,978
holding. Help with the water. Keep things quiet. Tell me

564
00:24:26,978 --> 00:24:30,078
if you hear people up there. He waited. That's it,

565
00:24:30,438 --> 00:24:32,938
I said. I got him a clean sweatshirt from a

566
00:24:32,938 --> 00:24:36,058
shelf. He folded it so carefully before he put it

567
00:24:36,058 --> 00:24:38,118
down that I had to find something else to look

568
00:24:38,118 --> 00:24:38,358
at.

569
00:24:38,723 --> 00:24:40,443
Vera called near dusk.

570
00:24:40,937 --> 00:24:42,837
Danny. Any room at the inn?

571
00:24:43,267 --> 00:24:45,307
I held the radio close to my ear.

572
00:24:45,715 --> 00:24:46,255
Still there?

573
00:24:46,673 --> 00:24:49,813
she asked. I pressed the button. You said you were

574
00:24:49,813 --> 00:24:50,753
trying on a coat.

575
00:24:51,121 --> 00:24:51,361
Yes.

576
00:24:53,164 --> 00:24:54,444
Before the mall closed.

577
00:24:54,886 --> 00:24:58,886
Eventually you're going to have to explain this interest

578
00:24:58,886 --> 00:24:59,806
in my shopping.

579
00:25:00,346 --> 00:25:03,366
Theo was watching me from the open tent. I let

580
00:25:03,366 --> 00:25:05,906
go of the button. Left her waiting this time. At

581
00:25:05,906 --> 00:25:08,186
five to nine, I took the flashlight from the shelf.

582
00:25:08,646 --> 00:25:10,306
Theo pulled on the clean sweatshirt.

583
00:25:10,641 --> 00:25:11,201
Can I see?

584
00:25:11,610 --> 00:25:12,090
he asked.

585
00:25:13,531 --> 00:25:16,411
I let Theo come up with me. He stood a

586
00:25:16,411 --> 00:25:19,031
little behind the hatch, keeping his weight off the bandaged

587
00:25:19,031 --> 00:25:22,931
leg. Across the highway, Parkview was barely visible against

588
00:25:22,931 --> 00:25:25,951
the sky. I found the tenth floor. Counted to the

589
00:25:25,951 --> 00:25:27,151
fourth window from the left.

590
00:25:27,585 --> 00:25:28,905
I always counted.

591
00:25:29,785 --> 00:25:31,925
Even when I already knew where to look. At nine,

592
00:25:32,365 --> 00:25:36,085
the flashlight came on. One. Two. Three. I answered with

593
00:25:36,085 --> 00:25:38,625
my own. My hands were steadier than they'd been the

594
00:25:38,625 --> 00:25:42,065
night before. I had water downstairs. There was another person

595
00:25:42,065 --> 00:25:45,685
waiting beside me, alive, who could hear something fall and

596
00:25:45,685 --> 00:25:46,425
help me pick it up.

597
00:25:46,816 --> 00:25:50,796
It came from the department store roof. One. Two. Three.

598
00:25:51,116 --> 00:25:53,436
Pointed across the highway. Toward her window.

599
00:25:54,796 --> 00:25:58,076
I lowered my flashlight. I wanted to blink again. Correct

600
00:25:58,076 --> 00:26:00,896
it somehow. Tell Lily which light was mine.

601
00:26:01,333 --> 00:26:04,393
But we had three flashes, and we had the emergency

602
00:26:04,393 --> 00:26:07,293
signal. That was all. I'd never taught her what to

603
00:26:07,293 --> 00:26:10,293
do when somebody else answered. My thumb rested on the

604
00:26:10,293 --> 00:26:13,533
switch while the department store roof went dark. I kept

605
00:26:13,533 --> 00:26:15,653
it there until I was sure I wouldn't press it.

606
00:26:16,133 --> 00:26:17,653
Theo looked from that roof to me.

607
00:26:17,990 --> 00:26:18,690
Who is that?

608
00:26:19,015 --> 00:26:19,695
he asked.

609
00:26:20,835 --> 00:26:23,115
I put the light in my pocket before I answered.

610
00:26:24,395 --> 00:26:24,955
The woman.

611
00:26:26,495 --> 00:26:28,075
The radio stayed off.

612
00:26:29,615 --> 00:26:30,615
In front of us,

613
00:26:31,715 --> 00:26:32,875
Lily's window went dark.

614
00:26:34,455 --> 00:26:35,815
Our goodnight was over.

615
00:26:37,315 --> 00:26:38,635
Somebody else had joined it.

616
00:26:40,215 --> 00:26:42,635
I stood there until Theo touched my sleeve.

617
00:26:43,226 --> 00:26:44,426
He was looking at the keys.

618
00:26:45,146 --> 00:26:47,346
The sock had come loose when I'd put the flashlight

619
00:26:47,346 --> 00:26:50,626
away. The last red tag hung against my hand.

620
00:26:50,997 --> 00:26:51,957
What's B3?

621
00:26:52,471 --> 00:26:54,051
he asked. I looked down.

622
00:26:54,751 --> 00:26:54,911
Why?

623
00:26:55,361 --> 00:26:58,821
That woman. She kept saying it. Down to B3.

624
00:26:59,221 --> 00:26:59,941
Get to the door.

625
00:27:00,364 --> 00:27:02,844
I closed my fingers around the tag.

626
00:27:03,461 --> 00:27:05,301
They weren't trying to get into a shop,

627
00:27:05,821 --> 00:27:06,261
he said.

628
00:27:06,918 --> 00:27:08,638
They were trying to get underneath it.

629
00:27:09,083 --> 00:27:12,143
I thought of Walt tapping the last key.

630
00:27:12,963 --> 00:27:13,423
Don't ask.

631
00:27:14,183 --> 00:27:17,083
Across the highway was my daughter. Across the roof was

632
00:27:17,083 --> 00:27:20,403
a woman copying her signal. And the thing that woman

633
00:27:20,403 --> 00:27:23,743
wanted was hanging from my belt. What did she think

634
00:27:23,743 --> 00:27:24,883
was behind that door?
